# terraform init drops provider binaries here — hundreds of megabytes, and
# platform-specific. Never committed.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform.tfvars
crash.log

# Also ignored, which is the less obvious call: a lock file generated on one
# machine records provider hashes for THAT platform only, so committing the
# darwin one would break `terraform init` on a Linux runner. These are
# reference modules that adopters copy into their own root, where they should
# generate (and commit) their own lock. A deployed root module would commit it;
# examples should not.
.terraform.lock.hcl
